1
00:00:00,566 --> 00:00:03,461
Meet Ordo, the AI maintenance engineer for

2
00:00:03,481 --> 00:00:07,428
your codebase, built on IBM watsonx.ai.

3
00:00:09,399 --> 00:00:11,376
Technical debt grows quietly.

4
00:00:11,396 --> 00:00:13,047
It piles up unseen,

5
00:00:13,067 --> 00:00:15,056
until it becomes an outage,

6
00:00:15,076 --> 00:00:18,342
slow delivery, or a security incident.

7
00:00:18,362 --> 00:00:20,292
Today's scanners produce long,

8
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:23,357
noisy reports, ranked by rule severity,

9
00:00:23,377 --> 00:00:26,236
with no business context and no fix path.

10
00:00:26,256 --> 00:00:27,847
So the list gets ignored.

11
00:00:29,866 --> 00:00:32,389
Ordo closes that gap in one pass.

12
00:00:32,409 --> 00:00:35,117
It analyzes a GitHub repository,

13
00:00:35,137 --> 00:00:37,614
ranks every finding by real risk,

14
00:00:37,634 --> 00:00:39,599
turns the list into a roadmap,

15
00:00:39,619 --> 00:00:40,864
and prepares the fix,

16
00:00:40,884 --> 00:00:43,079
the tests, and the pull request.

17
00:00:45,065 --> 00:00:47,076
The ranking is done by IBM Granite on

18
00:00:47,096 --> 00:00:48,690
watsonx.ai.

19
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:50,536
Every finding gets an urgency,

20
00:00:50,556 --> 00:00:51,569
business impact,

21
00:00:51,589 --> 00:00:53,148
and fix effort score,

22
00:00:53,168 --> 00:00:55,180
plus a plain English reason.

23
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,710
Let's see it live.

24
00:00:58,499 --> 00:00:59,895
This is Ordo's web app,

25
00:00:59,915 --> 00:01:01,195
running on Vercel.

26
00:01:01,215 --> 00:01:02,658
We'll scan a real project,

27
00:01:02,678 --> 00:01:04,908
Agora, straight from GitHub.

28
00:01:08,066 --> 00:01:10,786
I click Scan Repo Now and paste the repository

29
00:01:10,806 --> 00:01:11,576
link.

30
00:01:11,596 --> 00:01:13,410
While Bob streams the scan,

31
00:01:13,430 --> 00:01:16,266
Ordo reads the code through the GitHub API and

32
00:01:16,286 --> 00:01:18,272
runs five debt detectors.

33
00:01:22,099 --> 00:01:24,110
Seconds later, the dashboard.

34
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:25,399
Twenty findings,

35
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:27,709
nineteen of them high urgency,

36
00:01:27,729 --> 00:01:30,380
each scored by the Granite model for urgency,

37
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,738
impact, and effort,

38
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,732
with its reasoning attached.

39
00:01:37,865 --> 00:01:40,515
The overview breaks the debt down by category,

40
00:01:40,535 --> 00:01:42,454
shows repository stats,

41
00:01:42,474 --> 00:01:44,277
including zero test files,

42
00:01:44,297 --> 00:01:46,120
and lists the top issues.

43
00:01:46,899 --> 00:01:49,375
The roadmap is written by the model too.

44
00:01:49,395 --> 00:01:50,930
An overall assessment,

45
00:01:50,950 --> 00:01:53,540
then three phases the team can schedule.

46
00:01:55,443 --> 00:01:57,362
Open any issue to drill in.

47
00:01:57,382 --> 00:01:59,196
Ask why it is ranked here,

48
00:01:59,216 --> 00:02:01,391
and watsonx explains its reasoning in plain

49
00:02:01,411 --> 00:02:02,259
English.

50
00:02:03,833 --> 00:02:05,799
Then generate the fix.

51
00:02:05,819 --> 00:02:09,212
Ordo returns a step by step remediation plan,

52
00:02:09,232 --> 00:02:11,453
code hints, a testing strategy,

53
00:02:11,473 --> 00:02:13,206
and a pull request summary,

54
00:02:13,226 --> 00:02:15,714
ready to copy straight into GitHub with one

55
00:02:15,734 --> 00:02:16,605
click.

56
